---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SectionNav from '../components/SectionNav.astro';

const sections = [
  { href: '#principle', label: 'Principle' },
  { href: '#stakeholders', label: 'Stakeholders' },
  { href: '#integration', label: 'Integration model' },
  { href: '#responsibility', label: 'Responsibility' },
  { href: '#engagement', label: 'Engagement plan' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Human practices" description="See how AquaSense frames stakeholders, responsible implementation, feedback integration, equity, disposal, and future engagement.">
  <PageHero index="04" eyebrow="Human practices" title="Start with the system around the sensor." lead="A result can create anxiety, cost, and responsibility. AquaSense treats access to confirmation, communication, and remediation as design requirements—not downstream details." />

  <div class="page-shell">
    <SectionNav items={sections} />
    <article class="page-content">
      <section id="principle" data-reveal>
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span class="mono">Operating principle</span>
          <blockquote>Do not invite a community to detect a problem unless there is a credible path to confirm it and act.</blockquote>
          <p>AquaSense is a portfolio concept and has not been co-developed with affected communities. This page documents the questions, roles, and integration method that responsible future engagement would require.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="stakeholders" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 · Stakeholder system</p>
          <h2>Four perspectives, one testing journey.</h2>
          <p>Stakeholders are defined by the role they play, not treated as a generic “public.” The prompts below are questions to validate, not assumed answers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stakeholder-map">
          <div class="map-center"><svg viewBox="0 0 42 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 2C15 12 5 22 5 32a16 16 0 0 0 32 0C37 22 27 12 21 2Z" fill="currentColor"/></svg><b>AquaSense</b><span>screening pathway</span></div>
          <article class="stake s1"><span>01</span><h3>Community monitor</h3><p>What makes collection and interpretation feel trustworthy and manageable?</p></article>
          <article class="stake s2"><span>02</span><h3>Laboratory analyst</h3><p>What sample metadata is needed to make follow-up efficient and valid?</p></article>
          <article class="stake s3"><span>03</span><h3>Health communicator</h3><p>How should uncertainty and next steps be stated without false reassurance?</p></article>
          <article class="stake s4"><span>04</span><h3>Waste operator</h3><p>How should used cartridges be collected, classified, and transported?</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="integration" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 · Integration model</p>
          <h2>Feedback must change the design.</h2>
          <p>This hypothetical matrix demonstrates how future stakeholder input would be traced into requirements and revisions. It does not represent completed interviews.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="integration-list">
          <article><span class="source">Community monitor</span><blockquote>“A color by itself would make me nervous. Tell me what I am supposed to do next.”</blockquote><div class="integration-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="design-response"><b>Integrated response</b><p>Three named bands, redundant icons, and a written action beside every output.</p><em>Interface · R—01 / R—06</em></div></article>
          <article><span class="source">Laboratory analyst</span><blockquote>“A screening result is more useful when the sample context travels with it.”</blockquote><div class="integration-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="design-response"><b>Integrated response</b><p>Unique sample ID plus time, location, source type, and storage fields on the record card.</p><em>Traceability · R—05</em></div></article>
          <article><span class="source">Health communicator</span><blockquote>“Do not let ‘low signal’ become a claim that the water is safe.”</blockquote><div class="integration-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="design-response"><b>Integrated response</b><p>Use “low signal,” not “safe,” and repeat the limits of a single-analyte screen.</p><em>Risk communication · R—04</em></div></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="responsibility" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">03 · Responsible research</p>
          <h2>Risks live beyond the reaction.</h2>
          <p>The strongest failure modes are social as well as technical. Each risk needs an owner and a mitigation that can be evaluated.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-grid">
          <article><span class="risk-icon">!</span><div><h3>False reassurance</h3><p>A low signal could be mistaken for an all-clear despite unmeasured contaminants or a false negative.</p><b>Mitigation</b><p>Never use “safe”; show the analyte, scope, control state, uncertainty, and confirmation guidance together.</p></div></article>
          <article><span class="risk-icon">↔</span><div><h3>Unequal follow-up</h3><p>Screening can expose a problem without making certified testing or remediation affordable.</p><b>Mitigation</b><p>Launch only with funded confirmation and referral pathways defined by local partners.</p></div></article>
          <article><span class="risk-icon">⌁</span><div><h3>Sample location privacy</h3><p>Location data may identify a household, well owner, or community before they control the narrative.</p><b>Mitigation</b><p>Collect the minimum metadata, separate public reporting from identifiable records, and define data ownership first.</p></div></article>
          <article><span class="risk-icon">♻</span><div><h3>Material burden</h3><p>A sealed single-use format improves containment while creating plastic and reagent waste.</p><b>Mitigation</b><p>Minimize material, evaluate take-back logistics, and compare impacts against alternative screening workflows.</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="engagement" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">04 · Engagement plan</p>
          <h2>Ask in the right order.</h2>
          <p>Future work would pause at explicit decision gates. Technical development does not automatically authorize field deployment.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="engagement-plan">
          <li><span>Listen</span><div><h3>Define the decision</h3><p>Meet prospective community partners and ask whether lead screening is a priority, what is already working, and who should own results.</p></div><b>Gate: shared problem definition</b></li>
          <li><span>Co-design</span><div><h3>Prototype the full journey</h3><p>Test instructions, sample records, result language, referral options, and disposal—not only the cartridge.</p></div><b>Gate: acceptable workflow</b></li>
          <li><span>Validate</span><div><h3>Compare against standards</h3><p>Evaluate analytical performance with qualified laboratories and usability with representative users.</p></div><b>Gate: evidence threshold</b></li>
          <li><span>Govern</span><div><h3>Agree before deploying</h3><p>Set data ownership, communication, confirmation funding, incident response, and stop criteria with partners.</p></div><b>Gate: community authorization</b></li>
        </ol>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .principle-card { position: relative; padding: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); background: var(--navy); color: #edf9f5; border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; }
  .principle-card::after { content: '“'; position: absolute; right: 2rem; top: -5rem; color: var(--aqua); opacity: .15; font: 20rem Georgia, serif; }
  .principle-card .mono { color: var(--aqua); }
  .principle-card blockquote { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 820px; margin: 2rem 0; font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.1rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  .principle-card p { max-width: 700px; margin: 0; color: #b8d4d0; }
  .stakeholder-map { position: relative; min-height: 740px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; padding: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); background-image: linear-gradient(var(--line) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, var(--line) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 52px 52px; }
  .map-center { position: absolute; z-index: 3; left: 50%; top: 50%; translate: -50% -50%; width: 180px; height: 180px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: var(--lime); color: #062f35; border-radius: 50%; box-shadow: 0 0 0 20px color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper) 75%, transparent); }
  .map-center svg { width: 32px; color: var(--aqua-deep); margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .map-center span { font-size: .7rem; }
  .stake { width: min(100%, 310px); min-height: 220px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--paper-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1.2rem; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .stake:nth-of-type(even) { justify-self: end; }
  .stake:nth-of-type(n+3) { align-self: end; }
  .stake span { color: var(--coral); font: .65rem 'DM Mono', monospace; }
  .stake h3 { margin: 2rem 0 .7rem; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .stake p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .86rem; }
  .integration-list { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .integration-list > article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .35fr 1fr 50px 1fr; gap: 1.4rem; align-items: center; padding: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1.2rem; background: var(--paper-raised); }
  .source { color: var(--aqua-deep); font: 500 .68rem 'DM Mono', monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .integration-list blockquote { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.45; }
  .integration-arrow { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 38px; height: 38px; background: var(--aqua-pale); border-radius: 50%; rotate: -90deg; }
  .design-response { padding: 1rem; background: var(--aqua-pale); border-radius: .8rem; }
  .design-response p { margin: .3rem 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .84rem; }
  .design-response em { color: var(--aqua-deep); font: normal .6rem 'DM Mono', monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .risk-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; }
  .risk-grid article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: 2rem; background: var(--paper-raised); }
  .risk-grid article:nth-child(odd) { border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .risk-grid article:nth-child(n+3) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .risk-icon { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 48px; height: 48px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--coral) 16%, transparent); color: var(--coral); border-radius: 50%; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .risk-grid h3 { margin: .6rem 0 1rem; }
  .risk-grid p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .87rem; }
  .risk-grid b { color: var(--aqua-deep); font-size: .76rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .engagement-plan { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .engagement-plan li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 110px minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 2rem; align-items: start; padding: 2rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .engagement-plan li > span { color: var(--coral); font: 500 .7rem 'DM Mono', monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .engagement-plan h3 { margin-bottom: .6rem; }
  .engagement-plan p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .engagement-plan li > b { padding: .35rem .6rem; border-radius: 99px; background: var(--aqua-pale); color: var(--aqua-deep); font: 500 .6rem 'DM Mono', monospace; text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .stakeholder-map { min-height: auto; grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding-top: 220px; }
    .map-center { top: 110px; }
    .stake, .stake:nth-of-type(even) { width: 100%; justify-self: stretch; }
    .integration-list > article { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .integration-arrow { rotate: 0deg; }
    .risk-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .risk-grid article:nth-child(odd) { border-right: 0; }
    .risk-grid article:nth-child(n+2) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .engagement-plan li { grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; }
    .engagement-plan li > b { grid-column: 2; justify-self: start; }
  }
</style>
